        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.048,
            0.86,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.405,
            0.099,
            0.589,
            0.126
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.157,
            0.652,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": "Percentages are widely used in our daily life."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.188,
            0.822,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "Percentages are fractions with denominator 100. Percentages are denoted using the symbol ʻ%ʼ, pronounced ʻper centʼ. $X ^ { 0 } \\% = { \\frac { X } { 1 0 0 } } \\cdot$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.242,
            0.485,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "Fractions can be converted to percentages and vice versa. Decimals too can be converted to percentages and vice versa. For example, $\\frac{4}{10} = 0.4 = 40\\%.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.499,
            0.257,
            0.821,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_30_table_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.605,
            0.327,
            0.682,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": "\\frac { 4 0 } { 1 0 0 } = 0 . 4",
          "image_source": "images/page_30_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.37,
            0.821,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "We have learnt to find the exact number when a certain percentage of the total quantity is given."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.418,
            0.821,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": "When parts of a quantity are given to us as ratios, we have seen how to convert them to percentages."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.466,
            0.822,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": "The increase or decrease in a certain quantity can also be expressed as a percentage."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.514,
            0.821,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "The profits or losses incurred in transactions, and tax rates, can be expressed in terms of percentages."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.562,
            0.823,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": "We have seen how a quantity or a number grows when compounded. Interest rates are a common example of compounding. If p is the principal, r is the rate of interest, and t is the number of terms, then the total amount after the maturity period is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.803,
            0.822,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "A situation or a problem can often be solved by describing it using a rough diagram. We have learnt to estimate and do mental computations to solve problems related to percentages."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.877,
            0.914,
            0.909,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": "3 1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
